    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Byron originally belonged to Woods County before becoming part of Alfalfa County when Oklahoma achieved statehood in 1907.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byron%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The arrival of the Kansas City, Mexico and Orient Railway in 1902 helped Byron grow from a small settlement into a commercial hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
